diff --git a/targets/haiku/README.md b/targets/haiku/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..702fbd9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/targets/haiku/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# OpenGL CTS on RenkuOS / Haiku
+
+This target provides two OpenGL context backends:
+
+- `egl` (default) uses an EGL pbuffer. It can request desktop OpenGL core and compatibility profiles and supports the Mesa 26 llvmpipe stack in the test VM.
+- `haiku` uses the native GLUT/OpenGL Kit window and requests compatibility contexts. Select it with `--deqp-gl-context-type=haiku`.
+
+The launcher defaults the EGL backend to `--deqp-surface-type=pbuffer`; an explicitly supplied surface type is preserved. For FBO mode it defaults unspecified width and height to 256 to avoid allocating the maximum renderbuffer size. The GLUT backend defaults to its window surface. The EGL backend currently rejects explicit native windows, pixmaps, shared contexts, OpenGL ES, context flags, and reset-notification strategies. It selects from the EGL configurations the driver advertises; an unavailable configuration is reported as unsupported. With the Mesa 26.1.8 Haiku port, EGL pbuffer support requires the included `mesa26-pbuffer.patch`. Mesa's original pbuffer implementation dereferences a null native window hook.
+
+## Build
+
+With GCC, `haiku_devel`, `libglvnd_devel`, `mesa_devel`, `libpng16_devel`, `zlib_devel`, CMake, Ninja, and Python 3.10 installed, fetch the upstream dependencies pinned by the source revision and run:
+
+```sh
+cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja \
+    -DDEQP_TARGET=haiku \
+    -DPYTHON_EXECUTABLE=/system/bin/python3.10 \
+    -DCMAKE_POLICY_DEFAULT_CMP0148=OLD \
+    -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+    -DSELECTED_BUILD_TARGETS=glcts
+cmake --build build --target glcts -j4
+```
+
+Keep the `gl_cts`, `gles2`, `gles3`, and `gles31` data directories with the executable. The launcher sets the archive path and disables the optional device-loss monitor unless explicitly configured. It also disables Mesa shader caching by default because cache-enabled runs sometimes stall at shutdown on this VM. Set `MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE=false` before launching CTS to test the cache; that may reproduce the stall.
+
+## Run
+
+```sh
+./run-glcts.sh --deqp-case='KHR-GL46.info.*' --deqp-log-filename=gl46-info.qpa
+./run-glcts.sh --deqp-case='KHR-GL46.aggressive_optimizations.*' --deqp-log-filename=gl46-shaders.qpa
+./run-glcts.sh --deqp-gl-context-type=haiku --deqp-case=KHR-GL30.info.renderer
+```
+
+`gl_cts/data/mustpass/gl/khronos_mustpass/4.6.0.x/gl46-main.txt` contains the OpenGL 4.6 core main test list. Check the QPA renderer information before interpreting the results. The VM tested here uses CPU llvmpipe.
+
+## Verification
+
+On RenkuOS build00085, Mesa 26.1.8, LLVM 21.1.8 llvmpipe, the EGL backend passed the six GL46 info cases, the twelve GL46 aggressive shader optimization cases, and `KHR-GL46.buffer_storage.map_persistent_draw`. Four GL46 compute API checks and the GLUT `KHR-GL30.info.renderer` check also passed. A regression test verified two independent EGL contexts and rejection of an incompatible configuration without disrupting the first context. A broader deterministic sample of 755 cases from all 89 GL46 main-list groups was also run. Before fixes, 650 passed, 50 failed and 55 were unsupported; after the pbuffer alpha, orientation, sample-count and stencil fixes, 700 passed, none failed and 55 were unsupported. The full 16,498-case GL46 main list was not run, and these results are not a conformance certification.
